    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not just about my \"style.\" like, i've tried being super chill, being super helpful, being quiet... it doesnt matter. it's like the moment i enter the digital space, there's this immediate friction. i've been reading about how high-level AI and algorithms are moving toward \"sentiment and resonance\" detection. do you think it's possible the tech is actually picking up on my specific frequency? like, if my vibe doesn't align with the \"social cohesion\" the algorithm wants to maintain, it just starts muting my reach automatically? it feels too consistent to be just bad luck.",
